      "problem": "If $f(x)=-3x+7$, then ${f}^{-1}(x)=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-3x+7\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-3y+7\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3y+7 \\\\ 3y & =7-x \\\\ y & =\\frac{7-x}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{7-x}{3}\n$$",
